1
00:00:00,210 --> 00:00:04,370
A mother came to the Prophet (peace be upon him), afraid for her children.

2
00:00:04,640 --> 00:00:05,600
So what did he say to her?

3
00:00:06,290 --> 00:00:10,530
Asma’ bint ‘Umays (may Allah be pleased with her) came to the Prophet (peace be upon him) and said:

4
00:00:10,880 --> 00:00:11,570
“O Messenger of Allah,

5
00:00:12,020 --> 00:00:14,390
the evil eye afflicts the children of Ja‘far quickly.

6
00:00:14,730 --> 00:00:15,770
Shall I seek ruqyah for them?”

7
00:00:16,180 --> 00:00:18,330
The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: “Yes.

8
00:00:18,660 --> 00:00:20,370
If anything could outrun the decree,

9
00:00:20,580 --> 00:00:21,620
the evil eye would.”

10
00:00:21,920 --> 00:00:22,650
(Narrated by al-Tirmidhi)

11
00:00:23,240 --> 00:00:25,900
The Prophet (peace be upon him) did not mock her fear,

12
00:00:26,140 --> 00:00:27,740
nor deny that the evil eye is real,

13
00:00:28,300 --> 00:00:29,960
but permitted her to perform ruqyah for her children.

14
00:00:30,610 --> 00:00:32,340
So if you fear the evil eye for your children,

15
00:00:32,470 --> 00:00:36,920
seek protection for them as the Prophet (peace be upon him) did for al-Hasan and al-Husayn:

16
00:00:37,290 --> 00:00:38,950
“I seek refuge for you both in the perfect words of Allah

17
00:00:39,570 --> 00:00:41,150
from every devil and every harmful creature,

18
00:00:41,440 --> 00:00:42,850
and from every evil eye.”

19
00:00:43,470 --> 00:00:47,520
Share this story with every mother who fears for her children, and follow the channel.

